<title>USA: Amtrak orders GM diesel locomotives at $46 million.</title>
<headline>Amtrak orders GM diesel locomotives at $46 million.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amtrak has ordered 21 new diesel locomotives from the Electro Motive Division of the General Motors Corp. for about $46 million, Amtrak said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The division is based in LaGrange, Illinois, and London, Ontario, Canada.</p>
<p>Amtrak said the new locomotives would be delivered in the spring of 1998 and would be used in its western operations, replacing older GM locomotives, some of which are 20 years old.</p>
</text>
